\section{Conclusions}
\label{sec:concl}

\coffers are a new \change{VM-like} abstraction for cloud applications that use memory capabilities for secure isolation. \coffers include a library OS to minimize how much of the cloud environment is within the TCB. Multiple \coffers safely share an address space, allowing more efficient interaction of application components than when crossing current VM/container boundaries. Their asynchronous read/write and synchronous call interfaces allow capability-unaware, legacy code to run within \coffers.

