\subsection{Encoder and Decoder}


% 在我们的编码流程中，我们采用了常规图像领域的残差编码方法，并受到了GRASP-Net的启发。正如图3的部分（1）所展示的，这一流程分为两个主要部分，并遵循了从粗糙到精细的编码策略。首先，设初始输入的点云为 (x0,y0,z0)，它首先通过一个量化因子 scale_ratioscale_ratio 进行坐标量化，接着执行四舍五入操作以取整，并移除重复点。之后，我们使用G-PCC技术对量化后的坐标进行无损压缩，从而生成基础层码流数据（Base Bitstream）。在第二阶段，我们通过反量化操作 −1Q−1 获得更精细的几何坐标 (x1,y1,z1)，并将这些还原坐标与原始坐标 (x0,y0,z0) 进行差分，以获取残差信息 R，其中包含了量化过程中的细节信息。接下来的第三步，我们利用RAM模块（如图5所示）对残差进行特征提取和编码。RAM模块分为两个子模块：第一个是特征提取模块，它结合了KNN、Centering和PointNet技术，提取残差的潜在特征，其基本原理与GRASP-Net相似。第二个模块包含两次下采样过程，由稀疏卷积、卷积层下采样、三次IRN和SAM模块组成，进一步提取残差特征。其中IRN模块的计算与PCGCv2一致，而SAM模块则是一个由残差块组成的语义感知注意力模块，能够扩大感受野并提升下游任务的性能。我们的实验结果证明，SAM模块在提升下游任务性能方面起到了显著的作用。SAM的计算流程如下所示：
% 对残差进行两次特征提取后，我们会采用熵模型进行编码，最终得到增强层码流。

\textbf{Encoder.} We adopt the residual coding method commonly used in multimedia coding~\cite{pang2022grasp}. 
% particularly inspired by GRASP-Net. 
As shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:framework} (1), this process following a coarse-to-fine coding strategy. Suppose the input is denoted as $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$, and it first undergoes coordinate quantization, followed by a rounding operation for integer conversion. Then, we employ the G-PCC codec to compress the quantized coordinates, thus generating the BL bitstream. Lately, we utilize the de-quantization operation $Q^{-1}$ to obtain finer geometry coordinates $(x_1,y_1,z_1)$. These reconstructed coordinates are differenced from the original coordinates $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ to extract residual information $R$.
% , which leads to detailed information lost during quantization. 




The next step involves feature extraction and residual encoding using the RAM and Entropy Encoder, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:network} (a). The RAM is divided into two sub-modules: the first is feature extraction, combining KNN~\cite{guo2003knn}, Centering, and MSFEM (Fig.~\ref{fig:network} (g)) to extract latent features of the residual. Compared to PointNet, MSFEM is more adept at extracting multi-scale and local details information from the point cloud. The second module comprises two down-sampling stages, which utilize sparse convolution, three Inception-Residual Networks (IRN: Fig.~\ref{fig:network} (f)), and one SAM (Fig.~\ref{fig:network} (e)), to further refine the features of the residual. Constructed from Residual Blocks B (ResBlockB: Fig.~\ref{fig:network} (d)), the SAM expands the receptive field and enhances performance in downstream tasks. 
Our experimental results highlight the significant role of the SAM in improving the detection performance.
