\subsection{LLM autophagy}\label{app:autophagy}
\pdfig{8}{autophagy.png}{Example of LLM autophagy: 
numerals above coupons indicate sequential temporal points at which coupons manifest in their respective compartments. Coupons delineated by dashed borders represent responses produced by the Generative Artificial Intelligence (GAI) system. At time step 5, a purple coupon -- synthesized through the amalgamation of a blue and a red coupon -- is generated by the GAI system and added to online web resources. This coupon is then indexed by the Search Engine (step 6),
incorporated into the Training Set (step 7) and used as input for 
the Large Language Model (step 8). The resulting autophagous loop is denoted
by black arrows. }

Fig. \ref{fig:autophagy.png} provides an example of LLM autophagy. Starting from an empty system,
we describe the sequence of events at which coupons manifest in their respective compartments: 1) a red (bad) answer is posted on the Web; 2) a blue (good) answer is incorporated into the Training Set; 3) the bad answer is indexed by the Search Engine; 4) the good answer is fed into the LLM; 5) in response to a user's query, the GAI system generates a new random answer mixing the information contained in the blue answer coming out of the LLM and the red answer retrieved from the SE, producing a purple coupon which is subsequently added to online resources on the Web; 6) the purple coupon is indexed by the Search Engine; 7) information contained in the purple answer is incorporated in the Training Set; the same information is eventually used to train the LLM.


The aforementioned sequence of events engenders an autophagous feedback loop (illustrated in Fig. \ref{fig:autophagy.png} by black arrows), through which purple coupons may undergo iterative reinforcement. It is noteworthy that this process ultimately leads to the contamination of the training corpus, and by extension, the Large Language Model (LLM), with erroneous or misleading information -- an unintended consequence of retrieval-augmented generation techniques.


